# Product Brief

> The project's **product** layer (the counterpart to the constitution, which is the
> **engineering** layer). Written once per project, before the first feature. Each feature's
> `prd.md` REFERENCES this brief instead of repeating the product context — who the user is, why
> the product exists, the north-star metric. Keep it short and durable; whatever changes with
> each feature lives in the PRD, not here.

## Product

- [What the product is, in 1-2 sentences]
- [Why it exists — its reason for being]

## User

- [For whom — target user profile]
- [Jobs-to-be-done / core usage scenarios]

## Problem & Value Proposition

- [The core problem the product solves]
- [The value proposition — why this product and not the alternative]

## North-star Metric

- [The product's north-star metric — the single metric that best captures delivered value]
- [Distinct from per-feature metrics (those live in each `prd.md`)]

## Non-goals

- [What the product deliberately is NOT / does not do — at the product level]
- [Distinct from a feature's "Out of Scope": this is the product's boundary, not the phase's]
